<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Arranging books with grouping and fixed-position restrictions</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> There are \({@pblock@}\) different Mathematics books and \({@pother@}\) different Science books. In how many ways can they be arranged on a shelf if all the Mathematics books must stay together?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> \({@pn2@}\) different books are arranged on a shelf, with one particular book fixed at the start. In how many ways can the rest be arranged?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part (a): Grouping the Mathematics books together</b><br>
Treat the \({@pblock@}\) Mathematics books as <b>one single block</b>. Together with the \({@pother@}\) Science books, there are \({@pother@} + 1 = {@ptotal@}\) items to arrange, which can be ordered in \({@ptotal@}!\) ways.<br>
Within the block, the \({@pblock@}\) different Mathematics books can also be arranged among themselves in \({@pblock@}!\) ways.</p>
<p>Evaluate each factorial separately:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@ptotal@}! = {@exp_ptotal@} = {@val_ptotal_fact@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@pblock@}! = {@exp_pblock@} = {@val_pblock_fact@}\)</p>
<p>By the Fundamental Counting Principle, multiply the two counts together:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Total ways} = {@ptotal@}! \times {@pblock@}! = {@val_ptotal_fact@} \times {@val_pblock_fact@} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of ways} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b): Fixing one book at the start</b><br>
Because \(1\) particular book is fixed in the first position, only the remaining \({@pn2@} - 1 = {@prem2@}\) books are free to be arranged:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle ({@pn2@} - 1)! = {@prem2@}! = {@exp_prem2@} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of ways} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
